"""Lesson 18 student pages, checked source excerpts and UML sequence."""
STYLE+='''select{font:700 21px/1.5 "Segoe UI";padding:16px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;width:100%}#custom{width:24px;height:24px}#fixture-content{white-space:pre-wrap;font:20px/1.6 Consolas,monospace;color:var(--ink);background:var(--soft);padding:24px;border-radius:16px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}#notice:empty{display:none}.markdown-body{white-space:normal!important}.markdown-body li{margin:12px 0}#events li{font-size:19px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.json-view{max-height:460px}.workflow-step{scroll-margin-top:20px}'''
(PUBLIC/'style.css').write_text(STYLE,encoding='utf-8')
learn=[('Choose a discovery level','Author a project skill under .claude/skills/security-check/SKILL.md or a personal skill in the private user skills directory. The corresponding setting source controls discovery.'),('Write frontmatter and a workflow body','The app writes a real name, an editable single-line description, optional allowed-tools and trusted Markdown instructions. A specific description tells the model when the workflow is relevant.'),('Compare direct and model invocation','Direct /security-check dispatch loads the skill by name. A natural security-review request lets the model choose the matching Skill workflow. Both paths are observed with actual SDK results.'),('Pre-approve without confusing it with restriction','Compare allowedTools in query options with allowed-tools in SKILL.md. These pre-approve calls; explicit tools and the host target guard enforce the classroom access boundary.'),('Build release-notes from real history','The release exercise creates an owned classroom Git repository with two commits, exports actual git log, and lets /release-notes summarize that JSON. The model does not execute Git or inspect your working repositories.'),('Iterate on the description','Edit the description or select the tuned version, start a fresh session, and inspect the generated SKILL.md and completed calls. One successful invocation is an observation, not a statistical guarantee of trigger quality.')]
body='''<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Author</b><p>Name, description and workflow</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Invoke</b><p>/security-check or natural request</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Observe</b><p>Actual tools and findings</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Author and run a classroom skill</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Authoring experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="dispatch">Project skill · /security-check</option><option value="auto">Natural request · model chooses the skill</option><option value="frontmatter">Pre-approve tools in SKILL.md</option><option value="personal">Personal skill · user source</option><option value="missing">Missing source · plain review</option><option value="release">/release-notes · actual classroom Git history</option><option value="tuned">Tune the description · fresh model invocation</option></select><label for="description">Your security-check description</label><textarea id="description" rows="3" maxlength="400" aria-describedby="description-help"></textarea><p class="meta" id="description-help">Write one descriptive line of 20–400 characters. Name the task, trigger words and intended file. Selecting Tune loads an alternative description that you can edit. The skill name and read-only body remain controlled classroom templates.</p><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Write SKILL.md and run →</button></section><section class="note">The JavaScript scan fixture contains deliberately seeded issues and a fake training token. It is never executed or served. This is a teaching code review, not a comprehensive security audit. The release exercise uses its own private Git repository.</section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>Estimated cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p class="meta">Compare query allowedTools with SKILL.md allowed-tools. The host’s explicit tool list and exact-target guard remain in force for every mode.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Authored skill discovery</h2><pre><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Initialization lists discovered user-invocable skills. The full message is below; discovery metadata alone is not proof of invocation.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Completed tools, approvals and actual results</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Successful tool hooks record the actual targets. permissionRequests counts calls to the host fallback approval callback; intended pre-approved runs should not need it. Git hashes and subjects come from the real owned repository. Markers reflect actual response compliance. A missing required Read changes the host status to unverified_missing_read while preserving sdkStatus and original model text.</p></section><section class="step" id="fixtures-panel"><h2>Your generated SKILL.md files</h2><label for="fixture">File location</label><select id="fixture"></select><div id="fixture-content" role="region" aria-label="Authored skill contents">Run an experiment to inspect the generated skill.</div><p>The description is encoded as a YAML string. The student viewer displays the actual saved file separately; it is not copied into the model task prompt.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init message</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s runs</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Discovered classroom skills</th><th>Actual markers</th><th>Completed tools</th><th>Fallback approval requests</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages and tools</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section>'''
document('/','Author your <em>own SDK skills.</em>','Write a security-check workflow, compare invocation and approvals, then build release notes from actual Git history.',body,'<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Turn a reusable procedure into a discovered, invocable SKILL.md artifact.',cards(learn)+actions(('/run.html','Configure and run →'),('/architecture.html','Explore the UML →')))
env=(APP/'.env.example').read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip()
runsteps=[('Prepare Node and Git','Use Node.js 24+, npm, Git, your own Anthropic key and model access. Windows may need Git Bash. The release exercise creates its own owned repository and does not modify global Git identity.','cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson18-authoring-skills'),('Install and configure the key','Preserve an existing .env or copy the safe example. Enter your own key locally and keep it out of shared source.','npm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) {\n  Copy-Item .env.example .env\n}\nnotepad .env'),('Write and dispatch a project skill','Start the server and open port 3118. Edit the description, run Project /security-check, then inspect the actual generated SKILL.md and returned findings.','npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3118'),('Compare model invocation and pre-approval','Run Natural request, then Pre-approve in SKILL.md. Confirm actual file reads and no host fallback approval requests. allowedTools pre-approves; it does not restrict by itself.','npm run sample:env -- auto\nnpm run sample:env -- frontmatter'),('Compare personal discovery and missing sources','Run Personal with user as its source. Then run Missing source: files still exist, but classroom discovery is disabled and a plain review is requested.','npm run sample:env -- personal\nnpm run sample:env -- missing'),('Create release notes and tune descriptions','Run /release-notes against the exported actual classroom commits. Then select Tune, edit the description and inspect invocation in a fresh session. Keep the result as observed behavior rather than a guaranteed trigger rate.','npm run sample:env -- release\nnpm run sample:env -- tuned\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>The npm scripts load the optional .env explicitly. Existing shell variables take precedence. Restart after edits. No Managed Agents agent or environment ID is needed.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>If this app is already listening, startup prints its URL. If another service occupies the port, change PORT or stop that service. On Windows set CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH to the installed bash.exe if necessary. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. Check key/model access if a real query fails; errors are never replaced by a saved answer.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install, set your key, then compare fresh real SDK sessions.',body)
specs=[('Validate the editable description', 'src/agent.ts', 'c=validateConfig(c);', 'Accept only a listed authoring mode and a bounded single-line description. The browser cannot provide executable skill frontmatter or arbitrary filesystem paths.', 0, 1), ('Build YAML frontmatter and Markdown', 'src/agent.ts', 'const approvals=c.mode===', 'The trusted template supplies the skill name, an encoded student description, optional allowed-tools and the read-only workflow body.', 1, 4), ('Choose project or personal location', 'src/agent.ts', 'const d=directories(c,id),base=', 'Write real SKILL.md files in the owned project skills directory or the private user skills directory. Those locations correspond to selected setting sources.', 1, 4), ('Save the authored skill files', 'src/agent.ts', 'for(const file of files)await writeFile', 'Save actual filesystem artifacts before query. The host viewer shows their contents without copying them into the task prompt.', 1, 4), ('Export actual classroom Git history', 'src/agent.ts', 'const {stdout}=await git("log"', 'The release exercise creates two commits in an owned repository and exports their actual short hashes and subjects. The model reads that export without running Git.', 1, 4), ('Select the matching discovery source', 'src/agent.ts', 'settingSources:c.mode===', 'Project and user modes load their authored skills. The missing-source case uses [] while the files remain present.', 1, 2), ('Pre-approve through code or frontmatter', 'src/agent.ts', 'allowedTools:c.mode===', 'Session mode pre-approves Read, Grep, Glob and Skill. Frontmatter mode leaves only Skill in query allowedTools and pre-approves the file tools in SKILL.md.', 1, 2), ('Enforce the host tool boundary', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(name==="Read" &&', 'Explicit tools and exact-target checks enforce access independently of pre-approval. Only the authored sample and commit export can be read.', 2, 1), ('Choose slash dispatch or a natural request', 'src/agent.ts', 'const prompt=c.mode===', 'Direct /security-check and /release-notes dispatch are separate from model invocation on a matching natural security-review request.', 1, 2), ('Start the real SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run=query({prompt,options});', 'The SDK discovers authored skills and loads the selected workflow. Its native message and tool loop produce the actual report.', 1, 2), ('Record completed tools independently', 'src/agent.ts', 'completedTools.push({name:input.tool_name,target});', 'A successful PostToolUse hook records the actual file or skill target. The fallback callback separately records any unapproved tool request.', 2, 1), ('Verify the required data Read', 'src/agent.ts', 'const required=mode===', 'A successful SDK result alone is not enough. The host requires a completed Read of the correct sample or commit export; otherwise findings are labelled unverified. Original SDK status and text are retained.', 1, 4), ('Render findings as readable content', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer") renderMarkdown', 'Parse and sanitize real assistant Markdown. Keep findings, discovery, successful tools, approvals and Git evidence separate.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','Read guard','Private files']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={2:2,5:2,12:2}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 18 · Author skills → dispatch or match → observe actual tools</text>']
for x,label,colour in zip(xs,lanes,['#087fff','#8838ff','#00a977','#8838ff','#ee5425']):svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-150}" y="90" width="300" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1550" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 x1,x2=xs[a],xs[b];y=245+i*98;svg.append(f'<text x="{min(x1,x2)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="24">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x1} {y} H{x2}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg)+'</svg>',encoding='utf-8')
walk=''
for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen prompt selection and query workflow steps"></div>'+walk)
reference=[('Authoring surface', 'Students edit the description, while trusted templates fix the name, workflow and supported frontmatter. This teaches authoring without introducing arbitrary command hooks or dynamic shell substitutions. Full raw skill editing is outside this app.'), ('Project and personal levels', 'Project skills can be committed and shared. Personal skills apply across projects through the user configuration area. This lab uses a private user directory so it does not alter your existing personal skills.'), ('Approval is not restriction', 'allowedTools and skill allowed-tools pre-approve tools. They do not themselves constrain all tool use. The host also supplies an explicit tool list, disallowed tools and target checks. No shell, file edits or external web tool is exposed to the model.'), ('Description tuning', 'A specific description names the task and trigger terms. This lab records one fresh model invocation after tuning, not an evaluation dataset or a statistical proof of improved selection.'), ('Release-notes evidence', 'The host runs fixed Git commands only in a newly created private classroom repository, with per-command identity settings. The skill reads an export from actual git log; it does not inspect the course repository or run a model Bash command.'), ('Older commands and collisions', 'A flat .claude/commands/name.md file is an older command form; skills are the recommended successor. A command-file name can shadow bundled commands/skills. These compatibility and collision cases are reference material, not executed experiments here.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Follow actual application code and distinguish reference topics from live experiments.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 18 · Authoring your own skills\n\nBased on Lesson18_Authoring_Your_Own_Skills.pptx. Five linked web pages, large text, formatted answers and 13 source-linked UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson18-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson18-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations, use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson18-authoring-skills` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3118 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+ and model access are required.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file or copy .env.example. Enter your key locally; do not commit it. Restart after edits. Shell values take precedence over the optional file loaded by npm start.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nOn Windows, set the Git Bash path if needed. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. A second start recognizes this app; change PORT if another service occupies it.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'+''.join(f'{i}. {a}: {b}\n' for i,(a,b,c) in enumerate(runsteps[3:],1))+'\n```powershell\nnpm run sample:env -- dispatch\nnpm run sample:env -- auto\nnpm run sample:env -- frontmatter\nnpm run sample:env -- release\nnpm test\n```\n\n`sample` uses only the launching shell environment; `sample:env` loads the optional file. All queries are real and read-only. Prompt and context are fixed classroom choices, not arbitrary browser-supplied source paths.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for s in steps:readme+=f'### {s["number"]}. {s["title"]}\n\n{s["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{s["source"]}`, lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}. Selected excerpt.\n\n```typescript\n{s["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\nThe app never exposes the expanded internal prompt or inherited environment. Marker flags describe actual text, not complete instruction audits. Runtime skill files and private session context remain local. Private classroom directories are not an OS sandbox. Media, .env, dependencies and runtime files are excluded from Git.\n\n## References\n\n- [Authoring your own skills](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills)\n- [Authoring skill files](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 18 pages and 13 checked UML source snippets.')
